<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republic of Ireland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ireland, Éire, Poblacht na hÉireann</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ireland, also called the Republic of Ireland, is a country in Northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> consisting of 26 of the 32 counties of the island of Ireland. It shares its only land border with Northern Ireland, part of the United Kingdom. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-rising">Easter Rising</a> of 1916 and a War of Independence, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-irish-treaty">Anglo-Irish Treaty</a> of 1921 led to the creation of the Irish Free State in 1922 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> status. Acceptance of the treaty led to the Irish Civil War of 1922 to 1923. A new constitution of 1937 named the state Ireland and made it effectively a republic, and it was declared a republic in 1949. It joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Communities</a> in 1973.</p></div>
